Z||000005||84Bill||05-03-2001||12:57 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>What is your RPM at 35 and at 40</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Probably twisting between 2000 and 4500 RPM at that speed range in 4th. Got to be something spark related fuel would be mostly upper rpm range and constant.... EGR!!! will cause that! BUCKS RIGHT! had that problem found my EGR the culprit. To test it disconnect it and plug the hose.. will ping a bit but will not buck and stumble! go give that a shot!<P>you getting a lean error code?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
