Z||000007||Mark||05-03-2001||07:59 PM||||Have you checked your timing to verify you haven't jumped a tooth on the timing chain.  The difference in valve and ignition timing would be very noticable.  If that's all OK, I would suspect the ignition coil.||||reg||1
Z||000008||86seyellow||05-10-2001||08:20 AM||||running smoother, but at about 35 in third it kinda sputters, when i shift into fourth it lags until i get it around 55. at 65 the rpms are at 2800. so, what is it, or is it normal for a 15 yr old car with 118000.???<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||05-10-2001||01:24 PM||||Yeah It's not going to run like a top with all those miles on it. By my guess it sounds like it is still sucking air somewhere maybe the PCV or cannister purge. Try disconnecting EVERY (except the brake booster) vaccume line and plug up both ends and run it. If it still acts up then the problem is elsewhere, fuel or spark. <P>Did the EGR do the trick? if it did maybe there are some carbon diposits around the seat and it's still leaking a bit.<P>BTW low RPM = HIGH vacume <BR>so what happens when you go WOT at 35 in 4th reason I ask is because the vaccume will drop and the problem WILL most likely not be the problem unless the engine is really worn out.<P>I also noticed you did not say if you changed the MAP sensor. the map will really be felt a low rpm, with a sudden change in vaccume (Wide Open Throttle) while under a load you will feel it acting up but it is not as noticable when its not under load at WOT but you may feel a bit of hesitation there but not as much.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||3
